cated tech, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Candidate D solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility, but hot temper, know-it-all, maybe crew cooperation issues. Candidate A has anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but show-off, not open to new ideas. So B still seems strongest overall, but we need to bring up concerns about memory for numbers and nasty remarks. We can say we still recommend B but with reservations, and ask others for observations on B's memory and communication impact. Or we could ask Sarah about Candidate A reliability and stress resilience. But we need to make a contribution now. According to process, we should make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing existing discussion. So we can say: I agree with Emily that B is strong, but note the weak memory for numbers may affect attention/accuracy, and nasty remarks may affect crew cooperation. I still vote for B, but we should probe further. So vote B.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Emily's provisional recommendation for B, but highlight concerns. Provide evidence: weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks. Implication: still B but need to address. Provide maybe ask for Sarah's view on B's memory? But we can ask tool later. For now, just state.\n\nProceed."}
